# Dependency locks are pinned to LF, and nothing else is.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows development machines, so without
# this the locks are written LF by `uv pip compile` and checked back out
# CRLF. Recompiling then rewrites all ~1700 lines to LF, so the drift
# check that proves the locks match their .in files -- recompile, diff --
# reports the whole file as changed on a Windows runner, and Windows
# developers see the same phantom diff on a clean tree.
#
# Deliberately scoped to these four files rather than a repository-wide
# `* text=auto eol=lf`. Line-ending policy for the whole tree is a
# decision to take on purpose, not a side effect of adding a lock file:
# the wider rule would renormalise every tracked file and bury the
# engineering gates in a whole-tree diff.
requirements*.in    text eol=lf
requirements*.txt   text eol=lf
